.TH GIT-WORKFLOW-PULL 1 2026-10-03 git-workflow "git-workflow manual"
.SH NAME
git-rb-pull \- switch to a branch and bring it up to date with the remote
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git workflow pull
.RI [ branch ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Switch to
.I branch
(default: the current branch) and update it from its remote copy.
.PP
Protected branches (the main and dev branches) are only fast-forwarded,
and the command stops if they have diverged, so unpushed merge commits are
never flattened. Other branches are rebased onto the remote with
.BR \-\-autostash ,
unless the remote has nothing new. A branch that was rewritten after it was
pushed (by
.BR git\-workflow\-squash (1),
a rebase or an amend) is not rebased, since that would replay the old
commits on top: it stops and says to publish with
.BR "git workflow push force" .
.PP
With the default aliases
.RB ( "git workflow aliases install" )
this is also
.BR "git rb\-pull" ;
the 1.x name
.B rb\-pull
works after
.B git workflow
too.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-workflow\-sync (1),
.BR git\-workflow (1)
